WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:01.967
-I am so excited about this.

00:00:01.967 --> 00:00:03.803
Tonight,
we are coming to you live!

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:06.606
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.808
Live!
Whoa!

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.977
And this is very special --
our entire audience

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.312
is filled with Democrats
who are running for president.

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:14.881
So, unbelievable.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:19.686
Fantastic.
Congratulations.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.587
Yeah, just like the debate,
everyone here

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:23.857
gets 10 seconds to talk.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.958
And since it's NBC,
if you go past your time,

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:26.993
you're gonna hear this.

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:27.994
[ Dramatic tone ]

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.695
Okay.
That's the way it works.

00:00:29.695 --> 00:00:31.831
Now, the debate
was right here at NBC,

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.066
and there was a lot
of excitement in the building.

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:36.002
It felt
just like the Super Bowl,

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.471
you know, if 20 teams
played the game over two nights

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.172
and the winner wasn't decided
for another year.

00:00:40.172 --> 00:00:42.041
But besides that...

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:43.476
But it's true -- we're live,

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:46.479
and we just watched the first
Democratic debate down in Miami.

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:48.280
If you missed it,
here's what happened.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:51.050
There were 10 Democrats
on stage, and to qualify,

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:54.888
all a candidate needed
was to poll at 1% or higher.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:56.322
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.190
That's it?

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.493
One per--
I mean, even O.J. is at 2%.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.462
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:03.896
-But once it got under way,

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:05.498
something very interesting
happened.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:06.899
In his first question
of the night,

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:09.969
Beto O'Rourke decided
to start speaking Spanish.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:11.203
Watch this.

00:01:11.203 --> 00:01:12.638
-And it's gonna take all of us
coming together

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:15.074
to make sure that it does.

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:18.111
[ Speaking Spanish ]

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:25.918
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:28.421
-Cory Booker's face.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.123
Oh, Cory B-- yeah.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.625
Trump was watching like, "Crap.
Did I hit the SAP button?

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:33.960
What is it?
What is it?"

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.562
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:44.870
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:47.406
Then, when they called on
Bill de Blasio, he was like,

00:01:47.406 --> 00:01:51.177
"Uh, thank-a you-o.
I'm-a happy to be here-o."

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.812
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:55.148
Meanwhile, Cory Booker
saw Beto speaking Spanish

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:57.716
and decided to join in, too.
Watch him.

00:01:57.716 --> 00:02:05.658
-[ Speaking Spanish ]

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:08.962
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.163
-He sounds
like Arnold Schwarzenegger

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:11.564
learning Rosetta Stone.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:15.435
He's like...
[ Speaking Spanish loudly ]

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:17.136
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:20.473
[ Speaking Spanish loudly ]

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.809
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:25.478
Meanwhile, over on Telemundo,
they were speaking English.

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:26.912
-Really?
-It was unbelievable tonight.

00:02:26.912 --> 00:02:29.315
-Wow!
-Yeah, Beto and Booker

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.150
both spoke Spanish,
but it's not that crazy

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.852
because Miami has a large
Spanish-speaking community.

00:02:33.852 --> 00:02:35.555
I just hope that the next debate
is in Boston

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:36.856
so I can hear them say,

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:39.158
"We need free college
for anyone who is wicked smart."

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:40.492
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.492 --> 00:02:43.229
Later on, we got our first look
at one of the underdogs,

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:45.131
former Maryland Congressman
John Delaney.

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:47.100
Take a look at this guy.
Yeah.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.301
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:50.836
He looks like a talking thumb.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.836 --> 00:02:53.339
Well, as expected,
Elizabeth Warren and Cory Booker

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.575
did well tonight,
but I actually thought

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:57.976
Bill de Blasio
did a pretty good job, too.

00:02:57.976 --> 00:02:59.178
The New Yorkers are like,

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:00.480
"Where the hell's
this friggin' guy been?

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.181
Hey, whoa, hey!"

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:04.117
Meanwhile, later on --
[ Feedback ]

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.651
-Welcome back to "Today" --
-Sorry, sorry.

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:06.852
That's a mic.

00:03:06.852 --> 00:03:07.954
Can someone turn
Savannah Guthrie's

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:09.955
microphone off?
Thank you. Appreciate it.

00:03:09.955 --> 00:03:11.057
So, during the debate,

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:12.491
there were
some technical difficulties.

00:03:12.491 --> 00:03:13.860
Take a look at this.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.795
-Should there be a role
for the federal government --

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:17.930
-The mics are on.
-Everybody's mics are on.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.966
Think we had
a little mic issue in the back.

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:21.300
-Control room,
we've got contrary audio.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.568
-We had the --
I think we heard --

00:03:22.568 --> 00:03:25.138
Yeah, we have
the audience audio.

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:26.673
-What's happening?

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.874
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.874 --> 00:03:31.310
-Then Vladimir Putin was like,
"Is too easy."

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.578
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:34.613
"Is too easy."

00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:36.549
[ Laughs ]

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:40.586
Now, get this -- Trump tweeted
and called the debate boring.

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:42.288
But he still watched
even though he also said

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:45.024
it was a "very unexciting
group of people."

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:47.526
As opposed to the rock stars
he usually hangs out with,

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:49.295
like Mike Pence
and Steve Mnuchin.

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.329
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:51.664
But I think
I know why Trump's upset.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.299
He's probably
jealous of the Democrats.

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.468
You know, if you think about it,
they got to be on TV,

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:56.736
they got
to talk about themselves,

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:57.937
and they got to be in Florida.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.405
It's like, "These are
my three favorite things!

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:00.906
I can't believe it!"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:02.308
There's a lot going on
in the race,

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:04.076
and there's
so many Democrats running,

00:04:04.076 --> 00:04:06.879
it's hard to keep up,
so we thought we'd help you out.

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:07.913
Enjoy.

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:12.084
♪♪

00:04:12.084 --> 00:04:13.585
-♪ Bernie Sanders ♪
-♪ Tulsi Gabbard ♪

00:04:13.585 --> 00:04:14.921
-♪ Julián Castro ♪
-♪ Beto O'Rourke ♪

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:16.389
-♪ Elizabeth Warren ♪
-♪ John Delaney ♪

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:17.823
-♪ Kirsten Gillibrand
from New York ♪

00:04:17.823 --> 00:04:19.158
-♪ Cory Booker ♪
-♪ Andrew Yang ♪

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:20.593
-♪ I'm Bill de Blasio ♪
-♪ Tim Ryan ♪

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:22.095
-♪ Michael Bennet ♪
-♪ I'm Eric Swalwell ♪

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:24.263
-♪ Marianne Williamson ♪
-♪ Joe Biden ♪ [ Laughs ]

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:25.864
-♪ I'm Jay Inslee ♪
-♪ Kamala Harris ♪

00:04:25.864 --> 00:04:28.835
-♪ My name is Pete Buttigieg ♪
-♪ I'm Amy Klobuchar ♪

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.336
♪ And I approve this message ♪
-Yay!

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:31.570
-♪ I'm John Hickenlooper ♪

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.705
♪ Skinny kid
with a funny last name ♪

00:04:33.705 --> 00:04:35.041
-♪ Now,
who the hell's gonna beat me? ♪

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:36.542
♪ Their policies
are just insane ♪

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.976
-♪ Gun control ♪
-♪ Equality ♪

00:04:37.976 --> 00:04:39.312
-♪ Climate change ♪
-♪ Voting rights ♪

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:40.679
-♪ Campaign finance ♪
-♪ Free tuition ♪

00:04:40.679 --> 00:04:41.681
-♪ Living wages ♪

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:42.915
-♪ Will not deny
social justice ♪

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.283
-♪ Join the fight ♪
♪ Identify ♪

00:04:44.283 --> 00:04:45.718
-♪ A woman's right ♪
-♪ It's true ♪

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:47.820
-♪ No excuse ♪
-♪ We can't afford to lose ♪

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.722
-♪ Democratic candidates are
here to change the world today ♪

00:04:50.722 --> 00:04:51.957
-♪ I'm gonna change my slogan ♪

00:04:51.957 --> 00:04:53.493
♪ We'll sell many,
many more hats that way ♪

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:54.726
-♪ Focus on the future ♪

00:04:54.726 --> 00:04:56.362
-♪ There is nothing
we can't overcome ♪

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:59.131
-♪ Democratic candidates are
not afraid of Donald Trump ♪

00:04:59.131 --> 00:05:00.399
-♪ When people come after me ♪

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.034
♪ That's really, really,
really dumb ♪

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:04.770
-♪ Democratic candidates
will never defeat Donald Trump ♪

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:07.273
-♪ Extreme radical Democrats ♪

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:08.941
-Thank you very much.
-There you go.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:10.009
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:12.211
I hope that helps.

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:17.650
[ Applause ]

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.351
And did you
see the stage tonight?

00:05:19.351 --> 00:05:21.687
All the candidates were standing
in front of a fake White House.

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:23.356
Take a look at this.
Yeah.

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:24.457
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:25.691
Meanwhile,
inside the real White House,

00:05:25.691 --> 00:05:26.859
Trump was
looking out the window like,

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:28.927
"Why can't I see them?
Am I in the wrong --

00:05:28.927 --> 00:05:30.429
Am I in the Upside Down?"

00:05:30.429 --> 00:05:32.131
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:34.767
Earlier today, each candidate
got to spend a few minutes

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:36.435
doing a walk-through
on the stage

00:05:36.435 --> 00:05:38.204
just to check out the mics
and all that stuff.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:39.772
Most of them
wore suits and dresses,

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:43.042
but Ohio Congressman Tim Ryan
did things a little differently.

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:45.511
Watch this.
-All right, 2020 contender

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:47.045
Tim Ryan is on the debate stage
right now

00:05:47.045 --> 00:05:49.381
doing his walk-through.
That's gonna be happening

00:05:49.381 --> 00:05:50.917
through the course of the day.

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:52.084
-He's like, "Hurry up, dude!

00:05:52.084 --> 00:05:53.986
I got to get to the quad
for Frisbee golf!

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:56.989
I mean, what's going on?!"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:58.690
Guys, it seems like
there's so much going on

00:05:58.690 --> 00:05:59.759
in the news right now.

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:01.361
The Democratic debates
are this week,

00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:03.429
everybody's talking about
"Toy Story 4,"

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:05.297
Wimbledon is also starting up,

00:06:05.297 --> 00:06:08.834
and KFC just announced a new
Cheetos Chicken Sandwich.

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:11.570
There's a lot to go over,
so let's all just jump in,

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:12.839
cover it all at once.

00:06:12.839 --> 00:06:14.440
It's time for a News Smash.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.442
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:19.544
♪♪

00:06:19.544 --> 00:06:21.680
First up,
the Democratic debates.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:23.515
10 Democrats
went head-to-head tonight,

00:06:23.515 --> 00:06:25.551
and 10 more
will do the same thing tomorrow.

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:26.819
There are some
obvious front-runners,

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:29.322
but other candidates
aren't very popular at all.

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:32.124
You know what is popular?
"Toy Story 4."

00:06:32.124 --> 00:06:35.127
It's part of one of the most
successful film franchises ever.

00:06:35.127 --> 00:06:36.796
These movies
get people so emotional,

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:37.929
by the time
they leave the theater,

00:06:37.929 --> 00:06:39.331
they're an absolute mess.

00:06:39.331 --> 00:06:43.169
Speaking of absolute messes,
KFC's new Cheetos sandwich.

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:45.337
It's fried chicken
with Cheetos on top,

00:06:45.337 --> 00:06:47.273
drenched in
a Cheetos-flavored sauce.

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:49.642
If you're the kind of person who
plans on ordering this thing,

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:51.610
you know what
you probably won't be doing?

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:53.045
Competing at Wimbledon.

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:55.381
It's the biggest, classiest
tennis tournament of the year,

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:57.983
where players are required
to wear all white.

00:06:57.983 --> 00:06:59.952
You know who shouldn't
wear all white?

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:02.255
Anyone trying to eat
KFC's Cheetos sandwich.

00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:03.990
I mean, all the Cheeto dust,

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.257
and this thing
can't be good for you.

00:07:05.257 --> 00:07:07.927
The number of calories
probably goes all the way

00:07:07.927 --> 00:07:09.895
to infinity and beyond.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.895 --> 00:07:11.563
The "Toy Story" movies
have introduced us

00:07:11.563 --> 00:07:13.966
to so many great characters,
it's hard to keep up.

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:15.968
You know what else
is hard to keep up with?

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.870
All these Democrats.
They just keep going

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.705
back and forth and back forth.

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:21.340
You know what else
goes back and forth?

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:24.109
Tennis!
And qualifying for Wimbledon

00:07:24.109 --> 00:07:26.678
takes years
of blood, sweat, and tears.

00:07:26.678 --> 00:07:28.948
Speaking of tears, "Toy Story."

00:07:28.948 --> 00:07:30.917
These movies
can cause a lot of heartache,

00:07:30.917 --> 00:07:32.585
but if you really want
your heart to hurt,

00:07:32.585 --> 00:07:36.455
why not try
KFC's Cheetos sandwich?

00:07:36.455 --> 00:07:43.195
In conclusion, good luck,
good luck, good luck, good luck.

00:07:43.195 --> 00:07:48.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

